### ---------------------------------------------------
### Exercise 4 - Create tickets (POST /api/tickets)
### ---------------------------------------------------


### Exercise 4 - Task 1 & 2: Create a valid ticket (should return 201 Created)
# The backend sets status = OPEN and createdAt automatically
POST http://localhost:8080/api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Cannot access email",
  "description": "User cannot login to company email account.",
  "category": "Email",
  "priority": "HIGH",
  "createdBy": "amir@example.com"
}


### Exercise 4 - Task 2: Create another valid ticket (should return 201 Created)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Printer not working",
  "description": "Office printer on 2nd floor is offline.",
  "category": "Hardware",
  "priority": "MEDIUM",
  "createdBy": "siti@example.com"
}


### Exercise 4 - Task 2: Create an invalid ticket (should return 400 Bad Request)
# All fields are blank - validation should fail
POST http://localhost:8080/api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "",
  "description": "",
  "category": "",
  "priority": "",
  "createdBy": ""
}


### Exercise 4 - Task 3: Verify - Get all tickets after creating new ones
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets
